  "summary": "The Cornell Daily Sun reports on growing debate in Tompkins County, NY over Flock Safety ALPR cameras operated by Ithaca police and the county sheriff, with residents and legislators concerned about data sharing that could reach ICE via neighboring 287(g)-participating counties like Broome. Four county legislators opposed a state grant to continue Flock cameras, while Sheriff Osborne and IPD Chief Kelly defend the program, citing NY-only sharing, 30-day retention, and non-cooperation with ICE.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "I did not support [funding] Flock cameras and I believe there are other ways for us to use the funding.",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    },
    {
      "quote": "We only provide access to other agencies within NYS that have contracts with Flock",
      "paragraph_idx": 15
    },
    {
      "quote": "all agencies that access IPD's Flock data must comply with the same strict usage policies [set by IPD], which prohibit unauthorized use or sharing \u2014 including with federal agencies for immigration enforcement.",
      "paragraph_idx": 22
    },
    {
      "quote": "Ithaca currently has approved their Flock data access to 106 other law enforcement agencies.",
      "paragraph_idx": 26
    }
  ],
